        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "señor — \"sir,\" \"Mr.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin senior meant \"older,\" the comparative of senex, \"old.\" English took it raw as senior, and took the French descendant sieur — which is inside monsieur, \"my lord,\" and worn all the way down to English sir."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So señor, sir, senior and monsieur are one word, spread out."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ñ is the letter you met in the writing chapter. And this is what you say to get a stranger's attention politely, ahead of any of last chapter's repairs."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A way to address the person before you ask them anything."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "señor",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *señor*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "señor, por favor",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *señor, por favor*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "señor — ¿qué significa?",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *señor — ¿qué significa?*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What did senior mean? (Older.) Which English one-syllable word is the same root, worn down? (Sir.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
