              "text": "Two from last time, before anything new is added."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "pronunciation",
          "title": "Sounds you'll need",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say it once slowly, then at speed. see pronunciation reference."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "encantado — what you say on being introduced."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Latin incantare is in- plus cantare, \"to sing\" — to sing a spell onto something. English took it as enchanted, and kept the raw noun as incantation."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So the polite thing a Spanish speaker says on meeting you is, literally, \"I have been put under a spell.\" English does the identical thing and nobody notices: charmed, and delighted — de- plus lacere, \"to lure.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A man says encantado; a woman says encantada. You already have mucho gusto, which does the same job more plainly — either is right."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A full introduction now: greet, give both names, address them properly, and be charmed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "encantado",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *encantado*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "encantada",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *encantada*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "me llamo… encantado",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *me llamo… encantado*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Take incantare apart. (To sing a spell onto.) Which English word is it exactly? (Enchanted.) Which word you already had does the same job? (Mucho gusto.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
